                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "305c7c36-6389-38a1-8193-853948bef420",
                        "entry_id": "0d212376-f1da-3800-8a0c-05385367e9cc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not mitigated."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "91301eae-706d-3834-9c84-b8fb0664975b",
                        "entry_id": "0d212376-f1da-3800-8a0c-05385367e9cc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Total, complete, utter."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "emphatic",
                            "intensifier"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f4f4d5f-af2a-4141-8aab-0ebbfa71b115",
                                "sense_id": "91301eae-706d-3834-9c84-b8fb0664975b",
                                "text": "Their handling of the recent diplomatic crisis was an unmitigated disaster."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "077141e2-3761-4d74-ade5-f18c5c03479b",
                                "sense_id": "91301eae-706d-3834-9c84-b8fb0664975b",
                                "text": "Prichard, while keeping school, had the unmitigated gall to teach Greek, although he had never studied the subject."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4ee77dfc-7691-4fd1-87ec-594ee10d67cf",
                                "sense_id": "91301eae-706d-3834-9c84-b8fb0664975b",
                                "text": "In July 1938, that was sufficient to call down contempt and hatred on us, and brand us as men of unmitigated gall."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "41709311-773f-4df6-bd94-df922adfd0e5",
                                "sense_id": "91301eae-706d-3834-9c84-b8fb0664975b",
                                "text": "It requires the cunning of a chess master, the planning of a field marshal, the adroitness and polish of a premier of France, or, failing these, the sheer, unmitigated gall of your door-to-door salesman."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6a4eba39-022b-459f-9717-5ae402653442",
                                "sense_id": "91301eae-706d-3834-9c84-b8fb0664975b",
                                "text": "\"You don't care if people think you an utter blackguard? You don't care if she and your children have to beg their bread?\"\n\"Not a damn.\"\nI was silent for a moment in order to give greater force to my next remark. I spoke as deliberately as I could.\n\"You are a most unmitigated cad.\"\n\"Now that you've got that off your chest, let's go and have dinner.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "34cc0c14-bd0f-411d-81b3-d695ce6d9310",
                                "sense_id": "91301eae-706d-3834-9c84-b8fb0664975b",
                                "text": "\"The '720' has been out. We were really happy - it tested with no faults. There was a pleasant surprise it was an unmitigated success.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
